      },
      "message": "fix(sim): read a turning nose path's hidden rest as the turned work sees it\n\nA lathe Facing on a grooved bar was refused at the post: the envelope\nverdict's hidden-rest half read the groove floor across the spindle\n(a scan that never turns the work) and, once turned, 14 mm below the\nfaced band, as the Facing's own rest. The Profile kinds met the same\nfar-side reading, then the groove's inner corner a 0.8 nose cannot\nreach and the rough's own 0.25 leave.\n\nThe app now hands law (f) the spindle a turning nose op's kernel fitted\n(VerifyContext::lathe_axis, via turning::Frame::about). With it the\nhidden half (stock_sim::scan_turned) reads each hidden top on its\norbit about the spindle, excuses a top outside the axial band the nose\ncentres travel, excuses a crease the nose (grown by the leave) cannot\ntouch (the ridge law's own accessibility test), and lets the op's\nstock_to_leave stand. Gouge and visible halves, and every mill path,\nare unchanged; without a spindle the scan is bit for bit the old one.\n\nFixes #1408\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
