      "message": "fix(sim): excuse a hidden turned floor only when the pass never stood in its recess\n\nReview item on PR #1429 (head def62da): the band clause excused every\nhidden top out of the nose's reach along the spindle, so a turning pass\nthat went into a groove and stopped short of its floor posted clean\n(probe: z 35.5 / 36.0 into the 34..37 groove read rest 0.000).\n\nTurnedBand now also keeps each segment's station span. A hidden top is\nexcused only when it is out of reach AND no segment stands level (within\nthe reach) with its recess, the open span up the scan's Z to the part's\nnext surface over it. A pass that stood in the recess owns its floor.\nThe excuse holds only for a spindle along Z; any other spindle is judged\nwithout it (refuses, never passes). Milling paths are unchanged.\n\nPinned by turned_hidden_rest::a_pass_that_stops_short_of_the_groove_floor_it_entered_convicts\nand turning_hidden_floor::a_finish_that_stops_short_of_the_groove_floor_is_refused.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
